          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            (say on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            over a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            %em zeta function
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+continuation"} analytic continuation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\zeta_H(s) \coloneqq Tr(H^{-s})
          %p
            of the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -s
            power of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is suitably self-adjoint, is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
            of the
            = succeed "-powers" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -s
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+zeta+function"} Dedekind zeta function
            (or would be if there were something like a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laplace+operator"} Laplace operator
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spec%28Z%29"} Spec(Z)
            or more generally on an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+curve"} arithmetic curve
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+field+analogy"} function field analogy
          %p
            The exponential of the derivative of the zeta function at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
            also encodes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+determinant"} functional determinant
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regularization+%28physics%29"} regularized
            version (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+regularization"}> zeta function regularization
            ”) of the naive and generally ill-defined product of all eigenvalues. As such, zeta functions play a central role in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %p
            Generally, the values of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta_H(s)
            of interest in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            (when regarding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamilton+operator"} Hamilton operator
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+values+of+L-functions"} special values of L-functions
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#the_zeta_function The zeta function
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+differential+operator"} elliptic differential operator
            with positive lower bound
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+extension"} self-adjoint extension
            and write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \lt \lambda_1 \leq \lambda_2 \leq \cdots
          %p
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
          #ZetaBySeries.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em zeta function
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic function
              defined by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/series"} series
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ζ
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mi Tr
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %munderover
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo =
                                %mn 1
                              %mn ∞
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi λ
                                  %mi n
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi s
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\zeta_H(s)
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    Tr( H^{-s} )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\underoverset{n = 1}{\infty}{\sum} \frac{1}{(\lambda_n)^s}
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              where this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence"} converges
              and then extended by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+continuation"} analytic continuation
          %p
            (e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#DuistermaatGuillemin75"}> Duistermaat-Guillemin 75 (2.13)
            ,
            %a{:href => "#BerlineGetzlerVergne04"} Berline-Getzler-Vergne 04, section 9.6
            ) ).
          %h3#FunctionalDeterminant Functional determinant and zeta-function regularization
          %p
            Notice that the first
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta^\prime_H
            of this zeta function is, where the original series converges, given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi ln
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi n
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\zeta_H^\prime(s)
                  \=
                  \\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{- \ln \lambda_n}{ (\lambda_n)^s}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore one says (
            %a{:href => "#RaySinger71"}> Ray-Singer 71
            ) that the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+determinant"} functional determinant
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is the exponential of the derivative of zeta function of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            at 0:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                  %mi H
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  det_{reg} H
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\exp(- \zeta_H^\prime(0))
                  \\,.
          %p
            Via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+continuation"} analytic continuation
            involved in defining
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta_H(0)
            in the first place, this may be thought of as a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regularization+%28physics%29"} regularization
            of the ill-defined naive definition “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_n \lambda_n
            ” of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            as what is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+regularization"} zeta function regularization
          %p
            Conversely, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithm"} logarithm
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi H
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mi log
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi det
                    %mi reg
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z \coloneqq - \frac{1}{2}\zeta_H^\prime(0) = \tfrac{1}{2} log\,det_{reg} H
          %p
            is what is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+energy"} vacuum energy
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{-1}
            the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+propagator"} Feynman propagator
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = D^2
            has a square root
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            (a
            = succeed "-type" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eta+function"} eta function
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi det
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mi det
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mfrac
                    %mo ∂
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi s
                  %mfrac
                    %mo ∂
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi c
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  det H
                  \=
                  det (D^2)
                  \=
                  \\exp( \frac{\partial}{\partial s}\frac{\partial}{\partial c} \eta_{D}(0))
                  \\,.
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a{:href => "eta+invariant#RelationToTheZetaFunction"} eta invariant – Relation to zeta function
            for more on this.
          %h3#AnalogyWithNumberTheoreticZetaFunctions Relation to partition functions and number-theoretic zeta/theta functions
          %p
            By basic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            identities we have that
          #IntegralKernelExpression.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The series expression in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ZetaBySeries"}
              is equal to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mellin+transform"} Mellin transform
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mi k
                          %mo ≠
                          %mn 0
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi t
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mi d
                    %mi t
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\zeta_H(s)
                    \=
                    \\int_{(0,\infty)}
                    t^{s-1}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\lambda_k \neq 0}{\sum}
                    \\exp(-t \lambda_k)
                    \\right)
                    d t
                    \\,.
          %p
            (see e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#QuineHeydariSong93"} Quine-Heydari-Song 93 (8)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Richardson"} Richardson, pages 8-9
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BCEMZ03"} BCEMZ 03, section A.2
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ConnesMarcolli06"} Connes-Marcolli 06, theorem 13.11
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If one thinks of the operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
              of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanical+system"} quantum mechanical system
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi β
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mi k
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 0
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi β
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Tr(\exp(-\beta H))
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{\lambda_k \neq 0}{\sum}
                    \\exp(-\beta \lambda_k)
                    + 1
            %p
              is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
              of this system. Accordingly, prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IntegralKernelExpression"}
              says that the zeta function of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is obtained from its partition function by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi β
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi Tr
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi β
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mi β
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\zeta_H(s)
                    \=
                    \\int_{(0,\infty)}
                    \\beta^{s-1}
                    \\;
                    \\left(Tr(\exp(-\beta H)) - 1 \right)
                    \\;
                    d \beta
                    \\,.
          %p
            Further, by a change of integration variable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ≔
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\coloneqq x^2
            in the expression in prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IntegralKernelExpression"}
            one obtains
          #IntegralKernelExpressionInSquares.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The series expression in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ZetaBySeries"}
              is equal to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ζ
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi s
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi λ
                                    %mi k
                                  %mo ≠
                                  %mn 0
                              %mi exp
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %msup
                                %mi x
                                %mn 2
                              %msub
                                %mi λ
                                %mi k
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mi d
                            %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\zeta_H(s)
                    \&amp; =
                    2
                    \\int_{(0,\infty)}
                    x^{2s-1}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\lambda_k \neq 0}{\sum}
                    \\exp(- x^2 \lambda_k)
                    \\right)
                    d x
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = D^2
              is the square of a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              = succeed "-type" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
              = succeed ",then" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ±
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm \alpha_k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi α
                      %mi k
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_k = \alpha_k^2
              and hence in this case the series is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ζ
                              %mi H
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi s
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %munder
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi α
                                    %mi k
                                  %mo ≠
                                  %mn 0
                              %mi exp
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mi k
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mi d
                            %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\zeta_H(s)
                    \&amp; =
                    2
                    \\int_{(0,\infty)}
                    x^{2s-1}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{\alpha_k \neq 0}{\sum}
                    \\exp(- (x \alpha_k)^2)
                    \\right)
                    d x
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          %p By comparison one observes:
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The integral expression in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IntegralKernelExpressionInSquares"}
              is analogous to the expression of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+functions"} zeta functions
              in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+theory"} number theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
              as integrals of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+function"} theta function
              (for instance discussed
              %a{:href => "Riemann%20zeta%20function#RelationToThetaFunctions"} here
              for the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+zeta+function"} Riemann zeta function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi ζ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi s
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi d
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\hat\zeta_f(2 s)
                    \=
                    \\int_{(0,\infty)} (\theta(x^2) - 1) x^{2s-1} d x
                    \\,.
            %p
              Under this analogy the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+function"} theta function
              in the case of the differential operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi θ
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mi k
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 0
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi l
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta_H(x)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\underset{\lambda_k \neq 0}{\sum}
                    \\exp(- x \lambda_l)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is formally the same definition as that of adelic theta functions (e.g.
              %a{:href => "Iwasawa-Tate%20theory#Garrett11"}> Garrett 11, section 1.8
              )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundle"} determinant line bundle
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+determinant"} functional determinant
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+torus"} complex torus
              is a complex-analytic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+function"} theta function
              as above, quotiented by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+eta+function"} Dedekind eta function
            %p
              Early references explaining this include
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#AlvaresGaumeMooreVafa86"} Alvarez-Gaumé &amp; Moore &amp; Vafa 86
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AlvaresGaumeBostMooreNelsonVafa87"} Alvarez-Gaumé &amp; Bost &amp; Moore &amp; Nelson &amp; Vafa 87
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
              (
              %a{:href => "self-dual%20higher%20gauge%20theory#Witten96"}> Witten 96
              ).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#of_laplace_operator_on_complex_torus_and_dedekind_eta_function Of Laplace operator on complex torus and Dedekind eta function
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi τ
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}/(\mathbb{Z}\oplus \tau \mathbb{Z})
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+torus"} complex torus
            (complex
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+of+an+elliptic+differential+operator"} zeta function
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laplace+operator"} Laplace operator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi s
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi s
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi l
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi k
                          %mo +
                          %mi τ
                          %mi l
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi s
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\zeta_{\Delta} = (2\pi)^{-2 s} E(s)
                  \\coloneqq
                  (2\pi)^{-2 s} \underset{(k,l)\in \mathbb{Z}\times\mathbb{Z}-(0,0)}{\sum}
                  \\frac{1}{{\vert k +\tau l\vert}^{2s}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+determinant"} functional determinant
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mi Δ
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Im
                  %mi τ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi η
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi τ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn 4
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(
                  E^\prime_{\Delta}(0)
                  )
                  \= (Im \tau)^2 {\vert \eta(\tau)\vert}^4
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi η
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+eta+function"} Dedekind eta function
          %p
            (recalled e.g. in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Todorov03"} Todorov 03, page 3
          %p
            For more see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zeta+function+of+a+Riemann+surface"} zeta function of a Riemann surface
          %h3#analytic_torsion Analytic torsion
          %p
            The functional determinant of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laplace+operator"} Laplace operator
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            acting on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+n-forms"} differential n-forms
            is up to a sign in the exponent a factor in what is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+torsion"} analytic torsion
            of the manifold.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
          %div
